Z||000000||wxxo||08-09-2000||02:49 PM||||got a click click click sound when i push in the clutch. (4spd manual by the way) i just did a tranny swap. new one came out of an 85 gt. seems ok cept for the clicking noise. im thinking that its the throwout bearing. (they call it the throwout bearing because if something goes wrong with it youre better off "throwing out" your car as opposed to fixing it.haha) what do you all think??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||08-09-2000||05:09 PM||||Did you replace the throwout bearing with everything else?<BR>Where is the clicking coming from, the rear? Does it happen if the engine isn't running? Can you feel anything being transmitted through the pedal? Does the clicking happen WHILE you're disengaging the clutch, (pressing on the pedal) or while the clutch is disengaged-(pedal depressed)? Does it happen if you just apply light pressure to the pedal, making the throwout bearing come into contact with the pressure plate? Give me some more details, and we'll figure it out.....<BR>You DID put oil in that transmission didn't you?? I shipped it dry.....<P>-Taiji<p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 08-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||wxxo||08-09-2000||06:10 PM||||haha yea i put the oil in there haha. i used my old bearing. the tranny is great. im not thinking that it has anything to do with that. its that damn bearing. it was fine up until now so thats got me scratching my head. it only makes that noise when i push the clutch pedal down with the engine running. it doesnt matter if its in or out of gear. cant really feel anything being transmitted through the pedal. the clicking is coming from the rear where the tranny is. it only does it when the pedal is pressed from about 1/4 to all of the way in. thanks i dont think that i have left anything out but ill check back later to see what you have to say. thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||08-09-2000||06:14 PM||||When I replaced my flywheel I had the same problem. It is the throwout bearing. It went away within a week. That was a good thing too, Because I was not about to pull it back apart.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Taijiguy||08-09-2000||07:06 PM||||Go with the throwout bearing diagnosis, and pray you have the same luck as 64, and it goes away. Glad the trans worked out OK for ya. Did you run into any trouble with the swap?<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
